# PRD Workflow

The unit of delivery is a PRD that engineering can build without guessing.
Work moves through five phases. Do not skip one.

| Phase | Output | Gate to leave the phase |
|---|---|---|
| 0. Skeleton | `prds/<slug>.md` with every heading and TODO bodies, `stories/`, `glossary.md` | lint + `check_prd.py` pass |
| 1. Discover | Problem, Users, Goals, Non-goals filled. Notes in `research/` | Every goal has a metric |
| 2. Specify | Epics, story files, AC, NFRs, edge cases, rollout | `check_prd.py --strict` passes |
| 3. Validate | `docs/validation-<slug>.md` from `/pm-validate` | Verdict "Ready to decompose: Yes" |
| 4. Decompose | `docs/tickets-<epic>.md` from `/pm-decompose` | Dependency graph is acyclic |
| 5. Track | `docs/status-<date>-<epic>.md` from `/pm-report` | Shared with stakeholders |

## Commands to run

```bash
npx markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1          # lint every PRD, story and the glossary
python3 scripts/check_prd.py .        # headings + story structure + traceability
python3 scripts/check_prd.py . --strict   # also fails on TODO and unmeasured NFRs
```

Run both checks after every editing session. A red check means the phase is not done.

## Order of writing

1. Problem first. One paragraph, one named user, one cost of doing nothing.
2. Goals next, each with an ID (`G1`) and a number.
3. Non-goals before epics. They stop scope creep early.
4. Epics, each pointing at one goal.
5. Stories, one file each, each pointing at one epic.
6. AC, NFRs, edge cases, rollout, metrics, open questions.

## Decisions

When a trade-off is settled, write `decisions/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` with: context, options, decision, owner.
Link it from the PRD line it affects. Do not bury decisions in chat or comments.

## Research is input, not spec

Raw notes go in `research/`. Never paste raw transcripts into a PRD.
Pull out the facts, cite the research file, and move on.

## Hand-off

Jira and GitHub Issues are push targets. Edit in markdown, review, then push.
Never edit a ticket in the tracker without updating the story file first.
